# 📚 Stacks & Queues (Part 5) - Monotonic Queue & Sliding Window

## 📌 Introduction

A **Monotonic Queue** is a data structure that maintains its elements in a specific increasing or decreasing order.

It is especially useful when solving **Sliding Window** problems where we need to efficiently find the maximum or minimum element in every window.

These techniques are commonly used in coding interviews and competitive programming.

