# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Use a **Deque** to implement a Monotonic Queue.

✅ Store **indices**, not just values.

✅ Remove elements outside the current window.

✅ Remove useless smaller/larger elements.

✅ The front always represents the best candidate.

✅ Sliding Window Maximum can be solved in **O(n)**.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Storing only values instead of indices.

❌ Forgetting to remove expired indices.

❌ Using an increasing deque when maximum is required.

❌ Using a decreasing deque when minimum is required.

❌ Forgetting to check whether the deque is empty.

---

# 📝 Summary

- A Monotonic Queue maintains elements in a specific order.
- A Deque is commonly used to implement it.
- Sliding Window problems can be optimized using Monotonic Queues.
- For maximum values, use a **decreasing deque**.
- For minimum values, use an **increasing deque**.
- Sliding Window Maximum can be solved in **O(n)** time.

